vlan - virtual local area network.
partition - walled off section for data.

vlans can be in partitions and be defined by VIDs. Like vlan 1
vlan 1 and 2 for example cant talk together because they are sectioned off. like ports 1234 cant talk to 5678 because of a wall - 1234 | 5678
all devices unless told to be vlan aware will assume vlan1.